# The heavy part of the GPU image's Python, which the image does not carry:
# Dockerfile.gpu resolves it to the wheels in runtime.json, and runtime.py
# fetches and installs them when the node starts (see runtime.py).
#
# torch at CUDA 12.8: the oldest line with Blackwell kernels, and it runs on
# the 570 drivers most rented nodes still have. Pinned with its local version,
# which only the cu128 index carries: PyPI's own torch is newer and built for
# CUDA 13, and the first build of this image, which let pip choose, came out
# 2.14+cu130 - needing a 580 driver, and not seeing the GPU on half the nodes.
torch==2.11.0+cu128
# TileLang, for Ravex's quantization kernels (GPU-139): optional in Ravex,
# here because a GPU node is where they pay. Its compiler, nvcc, is in the
# image, from NVIDIA's apt repository (see Dockerfile.gpu).
tilelang==0.1.15
ml-dtypes>=0.5.1
